[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: AIM System Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-1
TITLE: Dual-channel ARINC 429 decode
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall decode ARINC 429 label 203 altitude words from two
independent air data channels (ADC-1, ADC-2).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-2
TITLE: Reject malformed words
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall reject (mark invalid) any altitude word with an incorrect
label or a failed parity check.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-3
TITLE: SSM discrimination
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall discriminate SSM status (Normal Operation, No Computed Data,
Functional Test, Failure Warning) and shall use only Normal Operation data for
altitude alerting and cross-side comparison.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-4
TITLE: Cross-side miscompare detection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall detect and latch a cross-side miscompare between ADC-1 and
ADC-2 per safety requirement SR-1 (see docs/safety/FHA.md).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-5
TITLE: Stale channel detection and fail-over
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall detect a stale channel per safety requirement SR-2 and shall
automatically use the remaining valid channel per SR-4 (see
docs/safety/FHA.md).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-6
TITLE: Approaching-altitude indication
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide an approaching-altitude indication when the aircraft
altitude is within the approach band of the selected altitude and not yet
captured.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-7
TITLE: Deviation alert
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide a deviation alert when a captured altitude departs
the deviation band for longer than the deviation persistence time per SR-3,
unless approach mode is active.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-8
TITLE: Selected altitude validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall accept and validate a pilot-selected target altitude, holding
the last valid value when an invalid selected altitude is received.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-9
TITLE: Deterministic, time-explicit operation
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall perform all alerting and monitoring functions deterministically
as a function of a monotonic time input (now_ms), independent of wall-clock
time or call rate.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-10
TITLE: Robust target-link framing
STATEMENT: >>>
The target firmware shall accept channel words, the selected altitude, the
approach-mode flag and step commands only from frames that pass sync and
checksum validation, and shall recover frame alignment after corrupted or
truncated bytes without losing a subsequent valid frame.
<<<
